{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455497-aberrant-mega-might-scale","id":1455497,"title":"[Aberrant] Mega-Might & Scale","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-24T01:59:01-07:00","id":1455497,"title":"[Aberrant] Mega-Might & Scale","content":"Okay, so the Mega-Lifting Mega-Edge seems obscenely powerful at a glance. Yes, you can't directly do damage with it, but since novas bend the laws of physics, ignoring the need for leverage and such, it would appear that a nova that boosts their Might scale for lifting to even just a 6 could lift a small city. I can't help but think there's something I'm missing, perhaps in the difficulty of the roll itself. It feels like a beginning character, if built right, could heft up a city, then drop it, which honestly would be cataclysmic for the city.<br /> <br /> From beginning to end, including difficulties, and spending successes on stunts, what would it take for a character with Might scale 6 to lift a scale 6 small city?<br /> <br /> What would it take for a character that used Mega-Lifting to boost their Might scale to 9 to lift a scale 6 small city?<br /> <br /> My ST is about to run two separate simultaneous games of Aberrant that exist side by side and I noticed that Mega-Lifting could technically be used to allow a starting character with Mega-Might 4 to achieve for instance a Might scale 9 for just lifting, and it seemed like this is either broken to the point where it could derail games (assuming the ST didn't just disallow such things for the sake of the game) or we are missing something critical that would make it a lot harder to do than it appears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 07-24-2021, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T02:38:01-07:00","id":1455499,"title":"","content":"Aberrant doesn't try to model realistic physics; and if someone tries the stunt that you're talking about (i.e., leveraging the ability to lift a lot into the ability to inflict harm), it's the Storyguide's job to put a stop to it: just because the letter of the rules can be abused doesn't mean that it isn't a violation of the <i>spirit</i> of the rules. <br /> <br /> In short, your right: technically, Mega-Lifting can be abused in the way that you describe; but the solution isn't too adjust the rules to address this potential abuse. It's to tell the players not to deliberately drop cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T04:21:33-07:00","id":1455502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455497-aberrant-mega-might-scale?p=1455499#post1455499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, your right: technically, Mega-Lifting can be abused in the way that you describe; but the solution isn't too adjust the rules to address this potential abuse. It's to tell the players not to deliberately drop cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Among other things because cities in general tend to be <b><i>full of people inhabiting them</i></b>, you know.<br /> Throwing them around tends to be a <i>mightly unrighteous</i> thing to do, with all the ensuing <b><i>collateral damage</i></b> and <b><i>mass casualties </i></b>involved.<br /> Heroes are usually the people <i><b>actively trying to put a stop</b></i> to this kind of stunt.<br /> Just sayin'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T14:56:05-07:00","id":1455533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455497-aberrant-mega-might-scale?p=1455499#post1455499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aberrant doesn't try to model realistic physics; and if someone tries the stunt that you're talking about (i.e., leveraging the ability to lift a lot into the ability to inflict harm), it's the Storyguide's job to put a stop to it: just because the letter of the rules can be abused doesn't mean that it isn't a violation of the <i>spirit</i> of the rules.<br /> <br /> In short, your right: technically, Mega-Lifting can be abused in the way that you describe; but the solution isn't too adjust the rules to address this potential abuse. It's to tell the players not to deliberately drop cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't argue against that. I know if I was the ST I'd consider the spirit of the rules.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm more looking to better understand the mechanics of lifting. If we ignore what's being lifted and just say the nova has Might scale 7 and wants to lift something with a Size scale 7 off the ground, would their target difficulty simply be a one?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T16:13:48-07:00","id":1455537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455497-aberrant-mega-might-scale?p=1455533#post1455533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't argue against that. I know if I was the ST I'd consider the spirit of the rules.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm more looking to better understand the mechanics of lifting. If we ignore what's being lifted and just say the nova has Might scale 7 and wants to lift something with a Size scale 7 off the ground, would their target difficulty simply be a one?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Inside the same scale there are different difficulties. Think like this, you, as a human I hope you are, can lift scale 1 objects, like a chair, a table, another person, a big rock or a motorbike, each one has a different difficult (1-5, kind of), same apply to scale 2 objects, a truck and a small car are the same scale, but with different difficulties when trying to lift.<br /> <br /> Its also not just about the weight, you may need to put in the math things like how hard it\u2019s to grab it (a 10kg box is harder to lift than a 10kg backpack) or how practical it is to lift it (a big empty box is harder to lift than a heavier gym weight because it\u2019s just too big to balance).<br /> <br /> In other words, to be able to lift an object with no effort you need to be capable of lifting one scale above, but it doesn\u2019t mean you can\u2019t lift it, it means you may need to roll some dice, and you may need to try again because you didn\u2019t grab it right or didn\u2019t balance it well, or what ever explanation you give narratively for not having enough successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}